      "content": "Here's a checklist of essential requirements for maintaining the cold chain during your international mRNA vaccine shipment from Belgium to Southeast Asia:\n\n* Confirm cargo flight schedule and plan for scheduled courier pickups.\n* Utilize approved (ISO 11923 or ANC Redux) temperature-controlled shipping containers with real-time monitoring systems.\n* Ensure the shipping containers are placed on a pallet with built-in cold storage and supported by still-airs or staking systems to minimize movement.\n* Label containers with tracking numbers and a critical temperature log sheet.\n* Plan for regular temperature checks (every 24 hours) using electronic goods monitors (EGMs) to monitor temperature tolerance of your transport equipment.\n* Prepare your team of flight attendants, handlers, agents, and end-users for exact injection of vaccines during every precautionary internal check step, ready capture images once per transit.",
